      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. To finish the thought you were on, how exactly can a chef control that moisture to ensure the temperature stays consistent across the whole surface? \n\nAlso, you mentioned earlier that the reaction can \"jump\" or happen in bursts. Even with the scientific explanation of thermal sinks, I'm still seeing these really weird, almost erratic patterns in my pan experiments where the browning seems to just \"behave\" unpredictably. Is there any other chemical reason besides moisture and sugar that would make the reaction act so... temperamentally?",
